[{:db/id "q-64600/selection/c4a44a92073201b15dc60d5b67ebe44f05900870950f834d5e33cc9b110f2d67" :answer/id #uuid "9201ed99-6036-5d7e-83ab-140ac9a3d798" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+2y=15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64600/selection/6518d7b2e80f7c72dcbeb6d72326528d77ec021f72f9e9057a3d658f35e905a6" :answer/id #uuid "f0bf89ae-11f6-5131-b017-01c2bd68e13e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+2y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64600/selection/3077d81c05dcc6e56a74b093f7d108ab8abd71e92e2593d5fcac7c26db785ef8" :answer/id #uuid "52d59049-6070-521d-8696-293de1bec4ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+4y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64600/selection/388dbb2db6ac6cbb231bdccc8d0b5aee1ee6947a9f9dc26b3dd5c6daa025907c" :answer/id #uuid "7977262c-2a7d-571a-bfa7-5236fa821be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+3y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64600/selection/08fb8a2e6b01d5240e2d0844f530f8da720f476fdd0314f92af421eefa1febd7" :answer/id #uuid "013bf829-6d33-5fcc-8bba-b99d51c60713" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+3y=15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64600/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "73e122ad-de35-50db-9d5a-999f0e97c8a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64600/selection/3077d81c05dcc6e56a74b093f7d108ab8abd71e92e2593d5fcac7c26db785ef8" :answer-field/choices ["q-64600/selection/c4a44a92073201b15dc60d5b67ebe44f05900870950f834d5e33cc9b110f2d67" "q-64600/selection/6518d7b2e80f7c72dcbeb6d72326528d77ec021f72f9e9057a3d658f35e905a6" "q-64600/selection/3077d81c05dcc6e56a74b093f7d108ab8abd71e92e2593d5fcac7c26db785ef8" "q-64600/selection/388dbb2db6ac6cbb231bdccc8d0b5aee1ee6947a9f9dc26b3dd5c6daa025907c" "q-64600/selection/08fb8a2e6b01d5240e2d0844f530f8da720f476fdd0314f92af421eefa1febd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64600" :question/id #uuid "0f27aa5d-1895-501d-94c1-b1e7c835ede1" :question/math-academy-id "q-64600" :question/problem "A particle of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=12\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$  The particle is also subject to the resistive force that's proportional to the particle's velocity with a damping coefficient $c=9\\,\\text{kg/s},$ and an external force given by $F(t)=15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{N}.$   \n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds.  If the particle moves with forced harmonic motion, what is the governing equation?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of forced harmonic motion with damping is\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-c{y}^{′}-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k,$ $c$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n3{y}^{″}=-9{y}^{′}-12y+15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+4y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64600/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e86899-2abb-5cca-9585-4a97e4630264"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64600"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64645/selection/6d99d75266c92c8a0ea983a803949bbce84bca3916fb26989df254f562005228" :answer/id #uuid "c4008f26-87f9-57e4-ab37-cda241f60295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\pi )=2({e}^{-3\\pi }-4)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64645/selection/4202b90c5e726acf2105cd5edf1634d7c9cc240f52bbc95eb4cd3c20d7ffe8ee" :answer/id #uuid "1adf96a0-5d6d-540d-a81e-ebbca61f89fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\pi )=2{e}^{-\\pi }({e}^{-2\\pi }-1)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64645/selection/309fc31b4d221db5ba476ef9e330908f986b8b96c10bf0ee3f18fd13f2515142" :answer/id #uuid "9e9b10be-246b-5a09-a794-829084d36f68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\pi )={e}^{-\\pi }(3{e}^{-2\\pi }-2)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64645/selection/49ce48e1f080171bcde1d85d7b956cced8ff741a60d71a4077c83af76b80d1f9" :answer/id #uuid "c474055e-f2dd-576f-a44c-e0046802f78d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\pi )={e}^{-\\pi }(4{e}^{-2\\pi }-1)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64645/selection/01fb19d6acc8163de8ff1bf329f3fd030f34f7766ed866ccce3fb1a8f4ccd6e0" :answer/id #uuid "91c780e1-ae5f-5238-81e6-aea0e0462c10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\pi )=(2{e}^{-3\\pi }-3)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64645/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d02bcfdd-4a16-5c27-b0d6-8fa4cc1b1524" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64645/selection/4202b90c5e726acf2105cd5edf1634d7c9cc240f52bbc95eb4cd3c20d7ffe8ee" :answer-field/choices ["q-64645/selection/6d99d75266c92c8a0ea983a803949bbce84bca3916fb26989df254f562005228" "q-64645/selection/4202b90c5e726acf2105cd5edf1634d7c9cc240f52bbc95eb4cd3c20d7ffe8ee" "q-64645/selection/309fc31b4d221db5ba476ef9e330908f986b8b96c10bf0ee3f18fd13f2515142" "q-64645/selection/49ce48e1f080171bcde1d85d7b956cced8ff741a60d71a4077c83af76b80d1f9" "q-64645/selection/01fb19d6acc8163de8ff1bf329f3fd030f34f7766ed866ccce3fb1a8f4ccd6e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64645" :question/id #uuid "79553835-e65f-59e1-aba2-8e979bcacb32" :question/math-academy-id "q-64645" :question/problem "The position $y(t),$ measured in meters, of a particle oscillating with forced harmonic motion with light damping is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=40{e}^{-3t},\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the particle is initially at the origin with zero velocity, find the position of the particle after $\\pi $ second." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to the equation of forced harmonic motion with light damping is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +17 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm 4\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}={e}^{-t}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t).\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are arbitrary constants of integration.\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(t).$\n\nThe external force is an exponential force. The constant factor in the exponent is $-2$, which is not a root of the auxiliary equation. Therefore, we assume a particular exponential solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha {e}^{-3t},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant to be determined. \n\nSubstituting ${y}_{p}$ into the differential equation and equating coefficients gives $\\alpha =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=2{e}^{-3t},\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-t}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)+2{e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nSince the particle is initially at the origin with zero velocity, the initial conditions are $y(0)=0$ and ${y}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\nSolving with these conditions for $P$ and $Q$ gives\n\n$$\nP=-2,\\,Q=1.\n$$\n\nSo our solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)+2{e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the position of the particle after $\\pi $ seconds, we substitute into the equation $t=\\pi .$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4(\\pi )-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4(\\pi ))+2{e}^{-3\\pi } \\\\  & =2{e}^{-\\pi }({e}^{-2\\pi }-1)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-64645/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5266e491-2718-56a9-b5a7-f4a86a8a01c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64645"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94231/selection/24ae96fa9643f0b3ccff732d92f35a647cc52c91c688368719096c2e27879869" :answer/id #uuid "a2d4c358-334b-51bf-bec6-6a5259d1b854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}-25y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94231/selection/ff63f36ca11af69de81401520d5a5f8d278e3182db3a73bbcbac0e7bbf838bf0" :answer/id #uuid "b2a087c2-9112-5b94-847c-670d9810cb0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+7y={e}^{-4t}+t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94231/selection/105814698e10869f0a90efc9f6518734a26b82e5d9fa23bec6fa18de96193136" :answer/id #uuid "8dd066cf-7eb7-59dc-bb41-a2f5256d6ce5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+4y={e}^{5t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94231/selection/4dedcd1d09af8bc657a8cfe84dfa017dffd5f77debe9c28a47b036b5031a4343" :answer/id #uuid "303e30dd-b69e-53a9-9d0d-258f01aa377c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\pi {y}^{′}+2y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94231/selection/3a827afdefa0cdffb674d51be598803d72f6ffb6086a602f5547a14a07565bfb" :answer/id #uuid "7dbf490c-d109-5c08-b66b-12ae85b46f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+36y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94231/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a015714c-c91d-5147-9e40-91e18340795f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94231/selection/ff63f36ca11af69de81401520d5a5f8d278e3182db3a73bbcbac0e7bbf838bf0" :answer-field/choices ["q-94231/selection/24ae96fa9643f0b3ccff732d92f35a647cc52c91c688368719096c2e27879869" "q-94231/selection/ff63f36ca11af69de81401520d5a5f8d278e3182db3a73bbcbac0e7bbf838bf0" "q-94231/selection/105814698e10869f0a90efc9f6518734a26b82e5d9fa23bec6fa18de96193136" "q-94231/selection/4dedcd1d09af8bc657a8cfe84dfa017dffd5f77debe9c28a47b036b5031a4343" "q-94231/selection/3a827afdefa0cdffb674d51be598803d72f6ffb6086a602f5547a14a07565bfb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94231" :question/id #uuid "c2c5477c-8ea5-5f3e-8509-189eb35b8466" :question/math-academy-id "q-94231" :question/problem "The function $y(t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t>0.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing forced harmonic motion without damping?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of forced harmonic motion without damping is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t).\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents forced harmonic motion without damping is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7y={e}^{-4t}+t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94231/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d29e7ead-5eae-5769-9502-7953d7018782"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94231"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94233/selection/28fb1d399bf8b3934b8a76e37cc790ddd507dd70b6570c9a62c53ec96e767137" :answer/id #uuid "fab92e09-6d90-5451-acc1-ecc8a417570d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2y=4{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94233/selection/8a4c41796d20257623712a0d51356428f2b45c8b014fcfb315f080f8cb78cdc0" :answer/id #uuid "c2113a69-96dc-55aa-88e2-bf4b065207d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+\\frac{5}{4}y=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94233/selection/143d6847e6fe4297c6b81b25110e5167c23c0b747a0ac0c6349fa11428a88daf" :answer/id #uuid "63ced7a7-284f-5b82-b18a-3621942228ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{5}{2}y=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94233/selection/31b873bf076ada7b8ff9585c606cf232777af1b282b6acff684e41397a6dbc8a" :answer/id #uuid "1ca71f6e-9d97-5127-a4ea-0f2947efdffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+4y=2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94233/selection/003734aefc1bc10c5c7aa647a2a360e6895a7591fedfb6b355941c98c7f465c3" :answer/id #uuid "5d5c7d27-eefb-5ad5-b5a7-3b2cd1d5b8e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}+5y=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94233/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4349e2-a0d1-5188-93fd-91e37f8b9c7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94233/selection/8a4c41796d20257623712a0d51356428f2b45c8b014fcfb315f080f8cb78cdc0" :answer-field/choices ["q-94233/selection/28fb1d399bf8b3934b8a76e37cc790ddd507dd70b6570c9a62c53ec96e767137" "q-94233/selection/8a4c41796d20257623712a0d51356428f2b45c8b014fcfb315f080f8cb78cdc0" "q-94233/selection/143d6847e6fe4297c6b81b25110e5167c23c0b747a0ac0c6349fa11428a88daf" "q-94233/selection/31b873bf076ada7b8ff9585c606cf232777af1b282b6acff684e41397a6dbc8a" "q-94233/selection/003734aefc1bc10c5c7aa647a2a360e6895a7591fedfb6b355941c98c7f465c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94233" :question/id #uuid "06c834d3-f655-589c-886c-ecaa57db3e34" :question/math-academy-id "q-94233" :question/problem "A particle of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=10\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$  The particle is also subject to the resistive force that's proportional to the particle's velocity with a damping coefficient $c=16\\,\\text{kg/s},$ and an external force given by $F(t)=4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{N}.$   \n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds.  If the particle moves with forced harmonic motion, what is the governing equation?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of forced harmonic motion with damping is\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-c{y}^{′}-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k,$ $c$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n8{y}^{″}=-16{y}^{′}-10y+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+\\frac{5}{4}y=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94233/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e86899-2abb-5cca-9585-4a97e4630264"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94382/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "836cdf4c-fbda-5284-8900-fdfb6624cc00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94382/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4d483b17-6630-52d2-85b7-8f7a08611b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94382/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "851de8ad-103b-5e46-a2f2-7e2457bf773e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94382/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "bc86b80a-8b5d-5519-8259-9d636519c27d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94382/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d1a62164-6cf3-502b-8661-5afa9e5a6b22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94382/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7111d041-05c2-50e2-bd88-a7a14f0cc3ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94382/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-94382/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-94382/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-94382/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-94382/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-94382/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94382" :question/id #uuid "ec54a4bc-6f62-5d4e-afc1-aa3f503d9658" :question/math-academy-id "q-94382" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+25y=24\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(25t+ϕ)+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$ It can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=25\\,⟹\\,\\omega =5.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =1$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nOnly III matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94382/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "813ec1d4-93ec-5a9e-996f-b2e672714927"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94382"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
